This is not open-source software. It is given to named people for research, and
the licence key in the application is the record of who holds a copy.


1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   Install and run Gene Studio on the computer your licence key names, for
   research, teaching and study, including work that is published. Results you
   obtain with it are yours: nothing here claims any interest in your data,
   your constructs or your findings.

   Keep copies for backup, and cite it as you would any tool
   ("analysed with Gene Studio, J.-Y. Sung").


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION

   a. Give it to anyone else — not the installer, not the application, not a
      licence key, not a part taken out of it.

   b. Change it, or make anything out of it, including a modified build or any
      other program containing part of this one.

   c. Take it apart to obtain its source — decompiling, disassembling, or
      unpacking the application bundle — except exactly as far as the law where
      you are says you may, and no further.

   d. Remove or alter the licence check, the copyright notices, or the
      attributions.

   e. Sell it, rent it, host it as a service, or put it inside a commercial
      product or a fee-charging service.

   Written permission means an email from the author saying so. Ask — for
   research use the answer is usually yes.


3. WHAT YOU GET, AND WHAT YOU DO NOT

   The software is provided AS IS, without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and
   non-infringement. The author is not liable for any claim, damage or other
   liability arising from the software or its use.

   Said plainly, because it matters in a laboratory: check what it tells you
   before you act on it. It reports what it computes from the sequence in front
   of it. It is a laboratory aid, not a clinical or diagnostic instrument, and
   a prediction is labelled as a prediction.


4. HOW IT ENDS

   The licence runs for the period the key states and ends when the key does.
   It also ends if clause 2 is broken. When it ends, stop using the software
   and delete your copies. Nothing you produced with it is affected.


5. WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER

   Gene Studio includes and relies on other people's work, which stays under
   its own terms and is not restricted by anything above:

   - the third-party components listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md — MAFFT
     (BSD 3-Clause), Aioli, SeqFold and its Rust dependencies (MIT), and
